sec.p:
$X_{\text {TAN}}^{1}, X_{\text {TAN}}^{2}, X_{\text {TAN}}^{3}, \ldots , X_{\text {TAN}}^{64}$ are the input feature sets for TAN ($X_{\text {TAN}})~X_{\text {TF}}^{1}, X_{\text {TF}}^{2}, X_{\text {TF}}^{13}, \ldots , X_{\text {TF}}^{64}$ are the input feature sets for TF ($X_{\text {TF}})~X_{\text {TH}}^{1}, X_{\text {TH}}^{2}, X_{\text {TH}}^{3}, \ldots , X_{\text {TH}}^{64}$ are the input feature sets for TH ($X_{\text {TH}}$)
\begin{align*} X_{\text {TAN}}& \in \{X_{\text {TAN}}^{1}, X_{\text {TAN}}^{2}, X_{\text {TAN}}^{3}, \ldots , X_{\text {TAN}}^{64}\} \\ X_{\text {TF}}& \in \{X_{\text {TF}}^{1}, X_{\text {TF}}^{2}, X_{\text {TF}}^{3}, \ldots , X_{\text {TF}}^{64}\} \\ X_{\text {TH}}& \in \{X_{\text {TH}}^{1}, X_{\text {TH}}^{2}, X_{\text {TH}}^{3}, \ldots , X_{\text {TH}}^{64}\}\end{align*}
where $y_{\text {TAN}}^{\text {HPLC}},y_{\text {TF}}^{\text {HPLC}},y_{\text {TH}}^{\text {HPLC}}$ are the HPLC values of TAN, TF, and TH, respectively.

The model for the fused dataset of TAN, TF, and TH in Fig. 8(b) can be represented as
\begin{equation*} y_{\text {TAN}}^{\text {HPLC}}, y_{\text {TF}}^{\text {HPLC}}, y_{\text {TH}}^{\text {HPLC}}=f_{\text {fused}}(X_{\text {TAN}}, X_{\text {TF}}, X_{\text {TH}})\end{equation*}
where $f_{\text {fused}}$ is the regressor function for the multiinput/output regressor.
